{
  "_note": "Two layers. (1) Index: each stage lists the broad syllabus area(s) it sits in (covers_syllabus_refs / syllabus_topic, as the source spec names them). (2) Coverage: _syllabus_items is the specification broken into its own atomic items, and each stage lists the item ids it teaches in covers_items, so coverage_check.py can say whether the WHOLE specification is taught. Top-level keys starting with _ are metadata, never stages.",
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "instructional_index_plus_itemised_coverage",
    "semantics": "covers_syllabus_refs is an index of the areas a stage is principally associated with; it does not claim exhaustive coverage of those areas, exam weighting, or official stage boundaries. Coverage is claimed only through _syllabus_items + covers_items, and only as far as coverage_check.py confirms (declared coverage, not verified teaching)."
  },
  "_items_source": {
    "document": "Council of Europe CEFR Table 1 (Global Scale) and Table 2 (Self-assessment Grid) for the 30 can-do items; standard Romanian-as-a-foreign-language grammar and vocabulary progression (as used by ILR/ACLro-aligned courses) for the grammar and vocabulary items. Ids are a stable scheme built for this course: RO-<level>-G<n> (grammar), RO-<level>-V<n> (vocabulary/topic), RO-<level>-CD-<skill><n> (can-do), since neither CEFR nor ILR publish a single numbered item list.",
    "url": "https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/table-1-cefr-3.3-common-reference-levels-global-scale ; https://europass.europa.eu/system/files/2020-05/CEFR%20self-assessment%20grid%20EN.pdf",
    "version": "CEFR (2001, reaffirmed by the 2020 Companion Volume); Europass self-assessment grid PDF as published 2020-05",
    "itemised_on": "2026-09-19"
  },
